.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
animated, moving image that is automatically moved, animated, and drawn 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "Events"
Things that happen to a sprite that might require intervention, such as collisions, completed animations, going offscreen, etc\&.\&.\&. will generate events\&. Events generated by sprites first go to any handlers attached directly to the \fBSprite\fP, then propagate up to the \fBSpriteLayer\fP and then the \fBEventManager\fP until they are handled\&.

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
translating events to JavaScript and running them through numerous handlers is expensive\&. Try to put your handlers as early in the propagation chain as possible\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "Inverse kinematics"
Use \fBaddAnimationIK()\fP to register a two-bone constraint on a supported animation rig\&. Update its target with \fBsetAnimationIKTarget()\fP and inspect the latest solve with \fBgetAnimationIKResult()\fP\&. The returned constraint ID is a pose modifier ID; use \fBremoveAnimationModifier()\fP to remove the constraint\&.
.SS "Helpers"
You can add helper functions or classes to do specialized animation behavior, and add visual effects during drawing\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
setAnimationHelper() 

.PP
\fBsetDrawHelper()\fP 

.PP
\fBsetPostDrawHelper()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "activateSubEntity (string entityName, string animationName = \fR'idle'\fP)"

.PP
activates a sub-entity with the specified name and animation This function activates a sub-entity within the Spriter animation system\&. Sub-entities are additional animated components that can be controlled independently of the main Spriter animation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentityName\fP The name of the sub-entity to activate 
.br
\fIanimationName\fP The name of the animation to play on the sub-entity
.RE
.PP
Sub-entities are typically used in complex character animations where different parts of the character (like arms, legs, or accessories) need to be animated independently\&. Each sub-entity can have its own set of animations and can be controlled separately from the main sprite\&.

.PP
When a sub-entity is activated, it will start playing the specified animation\&. The sub-entity will continue playing until it's deactivated or another animation is specified\&.

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
If the entityName or animationName is invalid, the function will fail silently 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Sub-entities are only available for sprites that support them (typically Spriter animations) 

.PP
The sub-entity will be positioned relative to the main sprite's position and rotation
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the sub-entity was successfully activated, false otherwise
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
Sprite::deactivateSubEntity() 

.PP
Sprite::isSubEntityActive() 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addAnimationDrawable (\fBDrawing\fP drawing, object options)"

.PP
attach an editable \fBDrawing\fP to an animation bone Use this overload to attach artwork, such as a weapon or a marker, that follows a bone as the sprite animates\&. Create the artwork with \fBpdg\&.createDrawing()\fP and the ordinary \fBDrawing\fP methods, such as \fBDrawing\&.addRect()\fP or \fBDrawing\&.addImage()\fP\&. The drawing uses coordinates relative to the selected bone; PDG positions, rotates, and scales it with the bone's final animation pose\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdrawing\fP The \fBDrawing\fP to attach\&. Its contents remain editable after registration, including through \fBElementRef\fP objects returned by its methods\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP An object selecting the bone, placement, and optional drawing settings\&. See \fBDrawing options\fP below\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A nonzero unsigned integer identifying the registration\&. Pass this ID to \fBsetAnimationDrawableEnabled()\fP, \fBremoveAnimationDrawable()\fP, or \fBgetAnimationDrawableError()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before registering artwork\&. The sprite's animations must have a fixed hierarchy: their active bones and bindings, and their parent relationships, must remain consistent across clips\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample: attach a marker to a hand\fP
.RS 4
This example assumes \fRsprite\fP is a Spriter sprite in a visible layer, with a \fRreference\fP animation and a bone named \fRhand\fP\&. Use the clip and bone names from your own artwork\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
if (!sprite\&.enableAnimationPose('reference')) {
    throw new Error(sprite\&.getAnimationRigError());
}

const artwork = pdg\&.createDrawing();
const marker = artwork\&.addRect(
    new pdg\&.Rect(\-3, \-3, 3, 3),
    new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.fillColor('yellow')
);

const drawableId = sprite\&.addAnimationDrawable(artwork, {
    bone: 'hand',
    placement: pdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll
});

// A later edit appears on the next draw; no new registration is needed\&.
marker\&.setAttributes(new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.fillColor('cyan'));

// When the marker is no longer needed:
// sprite\&.removeAnimationDrawable(drawableId);
.fi
.PP

.PP

.PP
\fBDrawing options (both overloads)\fP
.RS 4
Both overloads accept the following \fRoptions\fP fields\&. Only \fRbone\fP is always required\&. Use the numeric \fRpdg\fP constants for placement and stroke space; strings such as \fR"afterAll"\fP or \fR"local"\fP are not accepted\&.
.RE
.PP
Field  Type  Default  Meaning  \fRbone\fP  string or integer  Required  Bone name or zero-based bone ID\&. See \fBgetAnimationBoneNames()\fP\&.  \fRplacement\fP  integer  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll\fP\fP  Where to draw relative to the sprite's authored images; see the placement table below\&.  \fRslot\fP  string  Empty string  \fBImage\fP binding name\&. Required for slot placements; omit it for \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_BeforeAll\fP\fP and \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll\fP\fP\&. See \fBgetAnimationBindingNames()\fP\&.  \fRorder\fP  integer  \fR0\fP  Lower values draw first within the same placement and slot\&. Equal values preserve registration order\&.  \fRstrokeSpace\fP  integer  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationStroke_PortPixels\fP\fP  How line thickness responds to scale; see Stroke thickness below\&.  \fRbounds\fP  object  Omitted  Rectangle with finite numeric \fRleft\fP, \fRtop\fP, \fRright\fP, and \fRbottom\fP fields in bone coordinates\&. Must include all artwork and stroke extents\&.  \fRuncullable\fP  boolean  \fRtrue\fP without bounds; \fRfalse\fP with bounds  When true, prevents the artwork from being skipped based on its declared bounds\&.  

.PP
\fBPlacement\fP
.RS 4
A slot is a named image binding in the authored animation\&. It is separate from the bone that positions your drawing\&. Slot placements require \fRoptions\&.slot\fP to identify an existing image binding\&.
.RE
.PP
Constant  Value  Placement  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_BeforeAll\fP\fP  0  Before all authored images\&.  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll\fP\fP  1  After all authored images\&. This is the default\&.  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_BeforeSlot\fP\fP  2  Immediately before the named image\&.  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_AfterSlot\fP\fP  3  Immediately after the named image\&.  \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_ReplaceSlot\fP\fP  4  In place of the named image\&. Other images remain visible\&.  

.PP
\fBStroke thickness\fP
.RS 4

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fBpdg\&.animationStroke_PortPixels\fP\fP (0, default) keeps the \fBAttributes\fP line thickness in port pixels as the artwork scales\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fBpdg\&.animationStroke_Local\fP\fP (1) scales line thickness with the artwork, including element transforms, nested drawings, and layer zoom\&. For unequal horizontal and vertical scaling, the thickness multiplier is \fRsqrt\fP(abs(det(composedTransform))), the geometric mean of the scale factors\&. The stroke keeps a uniform thickness rather than stretching its outline differently along each axis\&.
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBBounds and visibility\fP
.RS 4
Bounds allow PDG to skip drawing artwork that is outside the visible area\&. When supplied, they must satisfy \fRleft\fP <= \fRright\fP and \fRtop\fP <= \fRbottom\fP\&. Omit bounds, or set \fRuncullable\fP to \fRtrue\fP, when you cannot provide a rectangle that safely contains all possible artwork\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
\fBDrawing\&.getBounds()\fP reports geometry bounds, which do not include complete stroke extents\&. Editing a drawing does not update the registration's declared bounds\&. Include enough room for strokes and later edits, or leave the registration uncullable\&. Visual bounds do not create physics or hit-test shapes\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBEditing and coordinates\fP
.RS 4
PDG retains the drawing's shared contents\&. Changes made through the original \fBDrawing\fP or its \fBElementRef\fP objects appear on subsequent draws\&. This overload does not invoke a JavaScript callback each frame\&.
.RE
.PP
Use \fBAttributes\fP to style drawing elements\&. Element transforms, the final bone and sprite transforms, and the layer's conversion to port coordinates are applied automatically\&. Opacity multiplies through the hierarchy\&. Do not transform the artwork to world or port coordinates yourself\&.

.PP
Nested drawings retain their child contents and map the child's bounds to the destination rectangle\&. \fBElementRef\fP objects also keep drawing contents alive\&. \fBDrawing\fP containment cycles are rejected\&.

.PP
\fBErrors and registration changes\fP
.RS 4
Registration throws if the pose is not enabled, the bone or slot is invalid, or an option has an invalid type or value\&. A slot is not allowed with \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_BeforeAll\fP\fP or \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Adding, removing, or enabling registrations during drawing takes effect after the current frame\&. A rendering failure disables the failing registration; \fBgetAnimationDrawableError()\fP returns its diagnostic\&. Register the artwork again to retry\&. A failed replacement leaves the authored image visible; a successful replacement suppresses that image even when the \fBDrawing\fP is empty\&.

.PP
Returned drawings and their images remain alive until their rendering finishes\&. \fBImage\fP opacity is restored after drawing, including on failure\&. Edits to shared drawing contents and pixels already drawn are not rolled back by a later error\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Headless builds retain registrations but do not draw artwork or invoke drawing callbacks\&. Use \fBisAnimationDrawingSupported()\fP to check drawing capability\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::addAnimationDrawable(function, object)\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::enableAnimationPose()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::setAnimationDrawableEnabled()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::removeAnimationDrawable()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::getAnimationDrawableError()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addAnimationDrawable (function callback, object options)"

.PP
choose or create artwork for an animation bone during drawing Use this overload when the artwork depends on the final animation pose or on application state at draw time\&. PDG calls your function synchronously during rendering\&. Return a \fBDrawing\fP to display it, or \fRnull\fP to draw nothing\&.

.PP
If you only need to edit an existing drawing, use the \fBDrawing\fP overload; those edits appear automatically without a JavaScript callback on each draw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcallback\fP A synchronous function called as \fRcallback(context)\fP\&. It must return a \fBDrawing\fP or \fRnull\fP\&. See Callback context below\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP An object selecting the bone, placement, and optional drawing settings\&. Both overloads use the same \fBDrawing options\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A nonzero unsigned integer identifying the registration\&. Pass this ID to \fBsetAnimationDrawableEnabled()\fP, \fBremoveAnimationDrawable()\fP, or \fBgetAnimationDrawableError()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before registering the callback\&. The sprite's animations must have a fixed hierarchy, as described in the \fBDrawing\fP overload\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample: show a hand highlight on demand\fP
.RS 4
This example assumes \fRsprite\fP already has an enabled animation pose and a bone named \fRhand\fP, as in the \fBDrawing\fP overload's example\&. Update \fRhighlightEnabled\fP from your application's input or update code\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const highlight = pdg\&.createDrawing();
highlight\&.addRect(
    new pdg\&.Rect(\-5, \-5, 5, 5),
    new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.fillColor('yellow')\&.fillOpacity(0\&.5)
);

let highlightEnabled = true;
const highlightId = sprite\&.addAnimationDrawable(function(context) {
    const hand = context\&.getTransform();
    return highlightEnabled && hand\&.alpha > 0 ? highlight : null;
}, {
    bone: 'hand',
    placement: pdg\&.animationDraw_AfterAll
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
The returned \fBDrawing\fP still uses coordinates relative to the bone\&. PDG applies the bone's transform; the callback does not need to reposition the artwork\&.

.PP
\fBCallback context\fP
.RS 4
The \fRcontext\fP object exposes these two methods:
.RE
.PP
Method  Result  \fRgetTransform(space)\fP  An owned transform object with \fRx\fP, \fRy\fP, \fRrotation\fP (radians), \fRscaleX\fP, \fRscaleY\fP, and \fRalpha\fP fields for the selected bone\&.  \fRcopyPose()\fP  An owned snapshot of the final animation pose\&.  

.PP
The optional \fRspace\fP argument uses one of these numeric constants:
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fBpdg\&.animationSpace_Local\fP:\fP relative to the bone's parent\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fBpdg\&.animationSpace_Rig\fP:\fP relative to the animation rig's origin\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fBpdg\&.animationSpace_World\fP\fP (default): in the owning layer's coordinates\&.
.PP

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
The context expires when the callback returns\&. Do not save it for later use\&. Transform objects and pose snapshots returned by its methods are independent copies and may be retained\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBCallback timing\fP
.RS 4
Rendering may run zero or multiple times per animation update\&. The callback can inspect the pose and choose, create, or edit artwork, but must not advance animation or integrate simulation\&. Keep time-dependent state changes in your application's update code\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBErrors and replacement images\fP
.RS 4
Registration uses the same validation rules as the \fBDrawing\fP overload\&. During drawing, a thrown exception or an invalid return value disables the registration and releases its callback\&. Returning \fRundefined\fP, an array, another kind of object, or a Promise is invalid\&. Use \fBgetAnimationDrawableError()\fP to read the diagnostic; register a new callback to retry\&.
.RE
.PP
For \fR\fBpdg\&.animationDraw_ReplaceSlot\fP\fP, returning \fRnull\fP or an empty \fBDrawing\fP successfully hides the named authored image\&. A failed callback or rendering failure leaves that image visible\&. Other authored images are unaffected\&.

.PP
Adding, removing, or enabling registrations inside a callback takes effect after the current frame\&. Edits to shared drawing contents are ordinary application changes and are not rolled back if the callback later fails\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Headless builds retain callbacks without invoking them\&. Use \fBisAnimationDrawingSupported()\fP to check drawing capability\&. See the \fBDrawing\fP overload for bounds, stroke thickness, and rendering behavior shared by both forms\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::addAnimationDrawable(Drawing, object)\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::enableAnimationPose()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::setAnimationDrawableEnabled()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::removeAnimationDrawable()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::getAnimationDrawableError()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addAnimationIK (object config, int order = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Register a two-bone inverse-kinematics controller\&. Validates a trial solve before registration\&. The controller runs in animationStage_Constraint on each evaluation, using the freshly sampled joint offsets\&. Inspect its result to distinguish unreachable, limited, and stretched solutions\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconfig\fP Configuration object described below\&. 
.br
\fIorder\fP Signed integer ordering within the constraint stage; default 0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A modifier ID usable with \fBsetAnimationIKTarget()\fP, \fBgetAnimationIKResult()\fP, and \fBremoveAnimationModifier()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&. The example assumes the rig has a contiguous shoulder/forearm/hand chain\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const ikId = sprite\&.addAnimationIK({
    root: 'shoulder', middle: 'forearm', tip: 'hand',
    targetX: 12, targetY: 8, space: pdg\&.animationSpace_Rig
});
sprite\&.setAnimationIKTarget(ikId, 14, 6, pdg\&.animationSpace_Rig);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBTwo-bone IK configuration\fP
.RS 4
Field  Default  Meaning  \fRroot\fP, \fRmiddle\fP, \fRtip\fP  Required  Bone names or IDs forming a contiguous parent-child-child chain\&.  \fRtargetX\fP, \fRtargetY\fP  0  Finite target position in the selected space\&.  \fRspace\fP  animationSpace_Rig  Local uses the root bone's parent frame; World uses the owning layer\&.  \fRrootLength\fP, \fRmiddleLength\fP  0  Zero derives length from the rig or child offset\&. Explicit positive lengths must match the joint offsets\&. Display widths are ignored\&.  \fRinfluence\fP  1  Finite blend weight from 0 to 1\&.  \fRbendDirection\fP  1  Integer +1 or -1 selecting the elbow side\&.  \fR\fBstretch\fP\fP  animationIK_NoStretch  Use animationIK_Stretch to allow extending toward out-of-reach targets\&.  \fRmatchOrientation\fP  false  Whether to aim the tip rotation as well as its position\&.  \fRtargetRotation\fP  0  Finite clockwise target angle in radians\&.  \fRrootMin\fP, \fRmiddleMin\fP  -Math\&.PI  Minimum local joint angles in radians\&.  \fRrootMax\fP, \fRmiddleMax\fP  Math\&.PI  Maximum local joint angles in radians\&.  
.RE
.PP
Nonuniform scales and reflections are supported when effective scales are nonsingular\&. Zero-length segments, incompatible offsets, invalid limits, and singular transforms are rejected atomically\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetAnimationIKTarget()\fP, \fBgetAnimationIKResult()\fP, \fBremoveAnimationModifier()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addAnimationModifier (function callback, int stage = \fR\fBanimationStage_PreConstraint\fP\fP, int order = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Register a procedural pose modifier\&. Modifiers run after source sampling and persistent overrides\&. They run by stage, then ascending order, then registration order\&. Each sees earlier successful edits\&. Keep evolving controller state in your own objects and apply it to each fresh pose; do not accumulate the previous final pose\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcallback\fP Synchronous function(view, context), described below\&. 
.br
\fIstage\fP \fBpdg\&.animationStage_PreConstraint\fP, \fBpdg\&.animationStage_Constraint\fP, or \fBpdg\&.animationStage_PostConstraint\fP\&. 
.br
\fIorder\fP Signed integer sort order within the stage; default 0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A nonzero modifier ID for removal or diagnostics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&. Inside callbacks, edit through the view\&. Perform playback, rig, physics, and layer changes outside the callback\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const modifierId = sprite\&.addAnimationModifier(function(view, context) {
    view\&.rotateLocal('hand', 0\&.15);
}, pdg\&.animationStage_PostConstraint);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBModifier callback arguments\fP
.RS 4
Argument / operation  Meaning  \fRview\&.copy()\fP  Return an owned pose snapshot (\fBanimation_pose_snapshot\fP)\&.  \fRview\&.getLocalTransform(bone)\fP  Copy a bone's parent-local transform\&. Bone arguments accept a name or numeric ID\&.  \fRview\&.getTransform(bone, space)\fP  Copy a Local, Rig, or World transform; Local is the default\&.  \fRview\&.setLocalTransform(bone, transform)\fP  Replace all six finite parent-local components; alpha must be from 0 to 1\&.  \fRview\&.rotateLocal(bone, radians)\fP  Add a finite clockwise rotation in radians\&.  \fRcontext\&.deltaSeconds\fP  Elapsed seconds; zero for explicit reevaluation\&.  \fRcontext\&.root\fP  \fBSprite\fP root transform in owning-layer coordinates\&.  \fRcontext\&.revision\fP  Pipeline revision as a decimal string\&.  
.RE
.PP
The view expires when the synchronous callback returns\&. Keep copies, not the view\&. The context is read-only\&. Return values are ignored, but returning a Promise is an error\&. An exception or invalid edit rolls back that callback's changes, disables it, and records a diagnostic\&. Registration/removal/source changes requested during evaluation take effect afterward\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremoveAnimationModifier()\fP, \fBgetAnimationModifierError()\fP, \fBaddAnimationIK()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::animationStage_PreConstraint\fP\&.
.SS "addFramesImage (\fBImage\fP image, int startingFrame = \fR\fBstart_FromFirstFrame\fP\fP, int numFrames = \fR\fBall_Frames\fP\fP)"

.PP
add one or more frames to the sprite from an \fBImage\fP or \fBImageStrip\fP 
.PP
References \fBpdg::all_Frames\fP, and \fBpdg::start_FromFirstFrame\fP\&.
