.PP
returns true if spriter events are enabled for this sprite 
.SS "\fBSprite\fP attachAnimationPhysicsPart (\fBPart\fP part, \fBPart\fP parent = \fRnull\fP)"

.PP
Register a physical \fBPart\fP in a physical rig's mass assembly\&. Adds the \fBPart\fP's existing mass to physics\&.getMass()\&. No other body's mass or inertia changes\&. The \fBPart\fP must belong to this \fBSprite\fP and already have a body\&. An accessory must have no \fBPart\fP parent, bone/slot/socket binding, or mounted \fBSprite\fP\&. Its current control mode is retained\&. Skeletal Parts previously detached from this rig can be registered again; they start Dynamic\&.

.PP
The optional parent records assembly hierarchy for subtree detachment\&. It does not create a joint, move a body, bind artwork, or claim an animation drive\&. Create joints explicitly with \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. For skeletal Parts, the nearest attached skeletal ancestor is automatic, and an explicit parent must match\&. For accessories, an omitted or null parent means an independent assembly member\&. Registering the same \fBPart\fP again is harmless; changing its parent requires detach\&.

.PP
Only registered bodies contribute to the total; arbitrary joint connectivity never adds mass\&. Whole-rig animation modes and recovery select attached skeletal bodies\&. An accessory keeps its own body control, responding through its joints\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpart\fP Physical \fBPart\fP owned by this \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.br
\fIparent\fP Attached \fBPart\fP used for assembly hierarchy; optional, default null\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires an enabled rig from \fBsetupPhysicsFromAnimationRig()\fP or \fBsetupAnimationPhysics()\fP, and a Chipmunk layer\&. Use \fBtransferPart()\fP to move a foreign \fBPart\fP into this \fBSprite\fP before registering it\&. Call outside animation modifiers and locked physics callbacks\&. Finish or cancel active recovery first\&. Explicitly release manual/Part-IK drives before reattaching skeletal bodies\&. Invalid edits throw before changing membership\&. Membership edits cancel pending mode-completion notices\&. The example assumes a rig with a hand \fBPart\fP and layer coordinates measured in centimeters\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const hand = sprite\&.findPart('hand');
const weight = sprite\&.createPart('weight');
const body = weight\&.setupPhysicsBody(10, 400); // kg and kg*cm^2
const grip = hand\&.physics\&.getState();
body\&.teleport(new pdg\&.Point(grip\&.x, grip\&.y), grip\&.rotation);
weight\&.setupCollider()\&.setBox(new pdg\&.Rect(\-10, \-5, 10, 5));
sprite\&.attachAnimationPhysicsPart(weight, hand);
hand\&.physics\&.createPivotJoint(body); // body\-local origins coincide
hand\&.physics\&.createGear(body, 1, 0); // retain their relative angle
// A 50 kg character now reports 60 kg\&.
sprite\&.detachAnimationPhysicsPart(weight); // drops it; total returns to 50 kg

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBdetachAnimationPhysicsPart()\fP, \fBisAnimationPhysicsPartAttached()\fP, \fBsetupPhysicsFromAnimationRig()\fP 
.RE
.PP

