.PP
attaches another sprite to this sprite at the specified attach point 
.SS "blendToAnimation (int animationId, number blendTime)"

.PP
Smoothly blend from current Spriter animation to a new Spriter animation by ID over the specified time\&. This function smoothly transitions from the current animation to a new animation by interpolating between the two over the specified blend time\&. The blend creates a seamless transition between animations\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIanimationId\fP The ID of the target animation to blend to 
.br
\fIblendTime\fP The duration of the blend transition in seconds
.RE
.PP
The blend operation interpolates between the current animation frame and the corresponding frame in the target animation\&. This creates a smooth transition that maintains the sprite's visual continuity\&.

.PP
The duration is a floating-point number of seconds\&. Progress is normalized from 0 to 1, and pausing freezes both playback and the visible blend\&. Starting a blend resumes paused playback\&. A completed blend emits one animation-blend-complete event on the normal update path\&. Starting another animation or blend cancels the pending completion of the old blend\&.

.PP
Invalid targets and nonfinite durations leave playback unchanged\&. Zero or negative durations complete on the next animation update\&. This method returns no value\&.

.PP
This is a phase-aligned Spriter blend, not an independently timed crossfade\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::blendToAnimation(string, number)\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::onAnimationBlendComplete()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::isBlending()\fP 

.PP
\fBSprite::getBlendProgress()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "blendToAnimation (string animationName, number blendTime)"

.PP
Smoothly blend from current animation to a new animation by name over the specified time\&. This function smoothly transitions from the current Spriter animation to a new Spriter animation by interpolating between the two over the specified blend time\&. The blend creates a seamless transition between animations\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIanimationName\fP The name of the target animation to blend to 
.br
\fIblendTime\fP The duration of the blend transition in seconds
.RE
.PP
The blend operation interpolates between the current animation frame and the corresponding frame in the target animation\&. This creates a smooth transition that maintains the sprite's visual continuity\&.

.PP
The duration is a floating-point number of seconds\&. Progress is normalized from 0 to 1, and pausing freezes both playback and the visible blend\&. Starting a blend resumes paused playback\&. A completed blend emits one animation-blend-complete event on the normal update path\&. Starting another animation or blend cancels the pending completion of the old blend\&.

.PP
Invalid targets and nonfinite durations leave playback unchanged\&. Zero or negative durations complete on the next animation update\&. This method returns no value\&.

.PP
This is a phase-aligned Spriter blend, not an independently timed crossfade\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
