.SS "deserialize (\fBDeserializer\fP deserializer)"

.PP
Restore selected state from a \fBSprite\fP record\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdeserializer\fP Reader positioned at a raw \fBSprite\fP record\&. An initial record supplies its state flags, frame artwork and playback cursor\&. It replaces existing frame images and collision masks, retaining shared resources\&. Independent and authored Parts restore their IDs/names, parent/binding links, artwork, animation tracks and bodies\&. Imported assets, clip/transition state, retained \fBDrawing\fP artwork and built-in rig IK are restored before their dependents\&. Previously retained Parts are detached when replaced; IDs removed before saving are not reused\&. Incremental updates use the destination layer's serialization flags\&. Resource resolution, validation or unsupported-format failures throw; discard the reader and destination after a failed load\&. This operation is not an atomic scene load\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::serialize()\fP, \fBSerializer::setResourceMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP detachAnimationPhysicsPart (\fBPart\fP part, boolean includeDescendants = \fRtrue\fP)"

.PP
Release a \fBPart\fP or subtree from the physics assembly\&. Removes the selected members' masses from the \fBSprite\fP total without redistributing any mass or inertia\&. Skeletal bodies become Dynamic and stop following animation; artwork continues following their physical bones\&. Body identity, pose, velocity, collider geometry and collision filters are retained\&. Joints within the selected set remain intact; every joint crossing its boundary is disconnected, including connections to external bodies\&. Retained disconnected constraint handles are safe to inspect but report inactive\&.

.PP
Descendants follow assembly hierarchy, including registered accessories\&. With includeDescendants false, surviving children are logically reparented to the nearest surviving ancestor; no replacement physical joints are created\&. Detached bodies are excluded from whole-rig control, recovery and aggregate mass edits\&. Address them directly through their \fBPart\fP's physics object\&.

.PP
If the selected root leaves, the remaining attached skeletal bone named root is preferred, otherwise the one with the most assembly descendants (ties use body definition order)\&. Whole-Sprite impulses and root follow use this replacement\&. At least one skeletal body must remain; \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP tears down the whole rig\&. Detaching a nonmember is a no-op\&.

.PP
This releases assembly membership, not \fBSprite\fP ownership\&. Parts and bodies remain alive while this Sprite/rig does\&. Disabling the rig removes all originally mapped bodies, including detached ones\&. Ordinary accessory Parts retain their bodies but stop contributing to the aggregate\&. Removing an accessory \fBPart\fP or its body also removes its membership\&. Mapped \fBPart\fP removal still requires rig disable; \fBtransferPart()\fP can instead release mapped bodies into another \fBSprite\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpart\fP \fBPart\fP owned by this \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.br
\fIincludeDescendants\fP Include the assembly subtree; optional, default true\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The same rig, callback and recovery restrictions as \fBattachAnimationPhysicsPart()\fP apply\&. Release manual/Part-IK drives on selected skeletal bodies first\&. Reattachment does not restore disconnected joints or snap the piece into place; restore the desired pose/constraints explicitly\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBattachAnimationPhysicsPart()\fP, \fBisAnimationPhysicsPartAttached()\fP, \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "detachSprite (\fBSprite\fP sprite)"

.PP
detaches the specified sprite from this sprite 
.SS "disableAnimationPhysics (number recoveryTime = \fR0\&.5\fP, int direction = \fR\fBrotationDirection_AsSpecified\fP\fP)"

.PP
Recover animation control before removing the physical rig\&. Uses the same collision-aware recovery as \fBsetAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP, defaulting to 0\&.5 seconds\&. The rig and its colliders remain active until recovery actually completes; \fBisAnimationPhysicsEnabled()\fP remains true meanwhile\&. Blocked or force-limited recovery may take longer than the requested duration\&. A new mode command cancels pending disable\&. Zero removes the rig immediately\&.

.PP
On completion, restores the \fBSprite\fP body's saved mode and collision filter and transfers the selected root body's linear/angular velocity\&. The explicit or generated rig's current total mass transfers to the single \fBSprite\fP body, keeping that body's previous single-body inertia\&. This is not a momentum-conserving merge\&. Mapped colliders and joints detach; retained mapped Parts remain body-free, and retained body handles stop contributing mass\&. Emits action_AnimationPhysicsRecoveryComplete with disabled true after teardown\&. Calling without an active rig is harmless\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIrecoveryTime\fP Finite nonnegative seconds; default 0\&.5, zero for immediate teardown\&. 
.br
\fIdirection\fP Rotation route; default rotationDirection_AsSpecified\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call outside animation modifiers and locked physics callbacks\&. Release any manual or \fBPart\fP IK drives explicitly before disabling\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP, \fBisAnimationPhysicsEnabled()\fP 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::rotationDirection_AsSpecified\fP\&.
.SS "disableAnimationPose ()"

.PP
Release the current pose rig\&. Disables animation physics and clears pose overrides, modifiers, IK, custom drawing registrations, and debug flags\&. Parts following the old rig become unbound\&. Ordinary \fBSprite\fP animation remains available\&. Calling when disabled is harmless\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call outside animation callbacks\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBenableAnimationPose()\fP, \fBisAnimationPoseEnabled()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean enableAnimationPose (string referenceAnimation)"

.PP
Enable pose access using a reference clip\&. Builds a stable rig from the selected Spriter entity and reference clip\&. The rig requires compatible bone, image, point, and box tracks with a fixed hierarchy\&. Nested entities and changing hierarchies are unsupported\&. On success, clears previous bone overrides, modifiers, IK controllers, custom drawings, and debug flags\&. A failed attempt preserves the previous enabled pose and records a diagnostic\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIreferenceAnimation\fP Name of an existing reference clip in the current Spriter entity\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True on success; false if the rig cannot be enabled\&. Read \fBgetAnimationRigError()\fP after failure\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Load Spriter data and select its entity first\&. Call outside animation callbacks and disable animation physics before replacing the rig\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
if (!sprite\&.enableAnimationPose('reference')) {
    throw new Error(sprite\&.getAnimationRigError());
}
const boneNames = sprite\&.getAnimationBoneNames();

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBdisableAnimationPose()\fP, \fBgetAnimationPose()\fP, \fBgetAnimationRigError()\fP 
.RE
.PP

