.SS "removeCollider ()"

.PP
Remove this owner’s collider\&. Idempotent\&. Restores shared NoCollider, removes native shapes, clears contact callbacks and detaches retained handles\&. Detached geometric queries preserve the final transform\&. 
.SS "boolean removePart (uint id)"

.PP
Remove an owned \fBPart\fP\&. Detaches any mounted Sprites in this \fBPart\fP's descendant chain\&. Direct child Parts stay owned by the \fBSprite\fP and lose this explicit parent\&. Retained references to the removed \fBPart\fP remain valid, keep local state, and stop automatic updates; its bindings and physics body are detached\&. Removing a mapped physical-rig \fBPart\fP requires \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP first; otherwise this operation throws without changing the graph\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIid\fP The \fBPart\fP ID, scoped to this \fBSprite\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if the \fBPart\fP existed and was removed; false for an absent ID\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPart::isAttached()\fP, \fBclearParts()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "removePhysicsBody ()"

.PP
Detach the optional physics body\&. Restores the physics property to \fBPhysicsBody\&.NoPhysics\fP\&. A retained body keeps its state, loses its owner/solver, and can be advanced with \fBPhysicsBody\&.step()\fP\&. Calling when no body exists is harmless\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody::step()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "resumeAnimation ()"

.PP
resumes the paused animation playback Continues a paused blend at the same progress\&. A naturally completed nonlooping clip resumes from its beginning\&. 
.SS "object sampleAnimationPose (string clip, number timeSeconds)"

.PP
Sample a clip without changing playback\&. Samples the authored clip independently of the live clock, bone overrides, and controllers\&. Does not emit trigger events or change rendering\&. Unknown or incompatible clips and nonfinite times throw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIclip\fP Name of a compatible clip in the current Spriter entity\&. 
.br
\fItimeSeconds\fP Finite sample time in seconds\&. Looping clips wrap, including negative times; nonlooping clips clamp to their endpoints\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An owned snapshot with the fields in \fBanimation_pose_snapshot\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const halfway = sprite\&.sampleAnimationPose('reference', 0\&.5);
console\&.log(halfway\&.bones\&.map(bone => bone\&.name));

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnimationPose()\fP, \fBseekAnimation()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "seekAnimation (string clip, number timeSeconds)"

.PP
Select a clip and time immediately\&. Cancels an active pose transition and legacy blend, while preserving the playback pause state\&. Validates the requested sample before changing the current selection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIclip\fP Name of a compatible clip in the current Spriter entity\&. 
.br
\fItimeSeconds\fP Finite sample time in seconds\&. Looping clips wrap, including negative times; nonlooping clips clamp to their endpoints\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&. Call outside animation callbacks\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.seekAnimation('reference', 0\&.25);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsampleAnimationPose()\fP, \fBtransitionToAnimation()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "serialize (\fBSerializer\fP serializer)"

.PP
Write selected \fBSprite\fP state to a data stream\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIserializer\fP Destination writer\&. A \fBSprite\fP in a layer uses \fBSpriteLayer::setSerializationFlags()\fP; an off-layer \fBSprite\fP uses \fR\fBpdg\&.ser_Full\fP\fP\&. Initial frame records include images, collision masks, frame layout and the fractional playback cursor when the corresponding animation and image flags are selected\&. Shared images retain their identity within the record\&. \fBSerializer::setResourceMode()\fP chooses embedded pixels or external image references\&. Programmed transforms/tweens and \fBPhysicsBody\fP state, including active drives, are included by the matching state flags\&. Timing values use floating-point seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
Updates with \fR\fBser_Animations\fP\fP (including \fR\fBser_Update\fP\fP) transfer sampled local \fBPart\fP transforms, reflection, constant movement and scheduled animations by \fBPart\fP ID\&. They preserve existing \fBPart\fP identities, parent links and artwork\&. This includes poses already solved by \fBPart\fP IK\&. The receiver can stop Layer animations and disable collisions to display only the received state\&. \fBPart\fP creation/removal, reparenting, artwork changes, IK controller configuration and \fBPart\fP body/constraint state require another initial snapshot; incremental \fBPart\fP records are not full physics checkpoints\&. A changed \fBPart\fP ID set is rejected\&.

.PP
Initial records also preserve independent Parts: IDs/names, parent links, local transforms, paused/active tweens, bodies and active drives\&. \fBPart\fP Image/Drawing content retains geometry, attributes, nested drawings and shared images\&. \fBDrawing\fP content is embedded in both modes; its images follow the selected resource policy\&.

.PP
\fBDrawing\fP colors and image transparency colors use eight-bit channels, with opaque alpha omitted\&. Floating-point colors can change by less than one channel step (1/255) when restored\&. \fBImage\fP pixel data is preserved exactly\&. \fBDrawing\fP geometry, pixel-space attributes (including thickness, text size, offsets and transform translation), and image subsections use the compact coordinate serializers\&. These can discard a fractional remainder smaller than 0\&.001 per encoded coordinate component\&. Rectangles encode their origin and size, so those small errors can accumulate at the opposite edge\&. Physics state, collision geometry, constraint anchors, IK inputs and Sprite/Part transforms retain their existing floating-point precision\&.

.PP
Packed boolean flags omit default values and absent payloads\&. Repeated images, \fBDrawing\fP storage and imported animation assets use shared object references within the same serializer stream\&. This preserves shared identity and avoids writing the same resource again; independently created objects remain distinct\&.

.PP
Imported SCML animations retain their shared model, selected entity/clip, floating-point playback time, pause/events, character maps, reference pose, bone overrides, blends and interrupted transitions\&. Bone-, artwork- and socket-bound Parts resolve against the restored rig\&. Built-in rig IK modifiers and retained \fBDrawing\fP registrations preserve their IDs, options and enabled state\&. Animation colliders continue following the restored pose\&.

.PP
Complete saves embed the imported document and its images and can load without the source files\&. Embedded XML is compressed losslessly with zlib when that makes it smaller; decompression is automatic\&. Documents are limited to 64 MiB before compression, and corrupt payloads or mismatched lengths cause a load error\&. External-reference saves omit the XML, resolve the original document path and verify that its contents have not changed; images use the selected resource policy\&. Missing or changed dependencies cause a load error\&.

.PP
Initial records preserve \fBCollider\fP shapes and shape IDs, frame/animation-source options, material overrides, collision filters, sensor/enabled state and contact-event opt-in\&. Compound-body associations, all \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP types, linked IK limits and active physical \fBPart\fP IK controllers resolve after all owners exist\&. Captured IK offsets and sampled drives survive; offsets are not recaptured from a deformed pose\&. Geometry is stored in both resource modes; frame images follow the resource policy\&. Restored colliders receive new process-wide IDs\&. Body angular-speed break thresholds, reference identities and notification latches also survive\&. Relative references must belong to the saved graph; a reported excursion does not repeat on restore\&. Native \fBPhysicsBody\fP break callbacks must be cleared before saving\&.

.PP
Initial records also preserve active physical rigs created from explicit configurations or generated skeletons\&. They save edited body/collider/constraint components, bone mappings, root selection, attached/detached membership, aggregate mass, desired poses, Kinematic/Dynamic/Driven modes, manual drive targets, rig drive settings and recovery progress\&. A pending recovery or disable resumes with its remaining duration and completion notification; a completed recovery is not reported again\&. Load into a Chipmunk-capable build and use a physics-enabled layer to continue simulation\&. A standalone restored \fBSprite\fP can be inspected before adding it to a layer\&. These records preserve engine state, not application callbacks; re-register application logic after loading\&. Save at an unlocked physics boundary\&. Layer initial restores validate the staged graph before replacing the live scene\&. Incremental motion updates are not rig checkpoints\&.

.PP
Callback collision filters/handlers are rejected; reinstall application handlers after loading\&. Solver contact caches and pending contact events are not saved, so loading rebuilds contacts and can produce new Begin events\&. A resumed simulation is not guaranteed to be bit-for-bit identical to an uninterrupted one\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Initial snapshots support frame-based and imported Sprites with independent or authored Parts\&. Standalone \fBSprite\fP saves reject attachments; save their owning \fBSpriteLayer\fP to retain mount relationships and cross-Sprite physical links\&. Older \fBattachSprite()\fP associations, modifier/drawing callbacks, callback helpers, custom easing, \fBFont\fP attributes and custom \fBDrawing\fP implementations are rejected\&. \fBDrawing\fP content requires a GUI-capable build\&. Layer collections can be restored with \fBSpriteLayer::deserialize()\fP\&. Discard the writer after a save error\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
// sprite is an off\-layer Sprite with frame or imported artwork\&.
const writer = new pdg\&.Serializer();
writer\&.setResourceMode(pdg\&.serialization_Complete);
writer\&.serialize_obj(sprite);
const reader = new pdg\&.Deserializer();
reader\&.setDataPtr(writer\&.getDataPtr());
const restored = reader\&.deserialize_obj();  // a new pdg\&.Sprite
.fi
.PP
 Raw \fBserialize()\fP/deserialize() calls instead replace state on an existing \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::deserialize()\fP, \fBSprite::getSerializedSize()\fP, \fBSerializer::setResourceMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "setAnimationBoneTransform (string name, object transform)"

.PP
Override a bone's parent-local transform\&. Replaces all six transform components; this is an absolute local override, not an accumulated offset\&. It persists across updates and clip changes until cleared or the rig is replaced\&. Invalid names or nonfinite values throw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Exact bone name in the current rig\&. 
.br
\fItransform\fP An object containing finite \fRx\fP, \fRy\fP, \fRrotation\fP (radians), \fRscaleX\fP, \fRscaleY\fP, and \fRalpha\fP (0 to 1) values\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&. Call outside modifiers; use their borrowed view to edit a pose during evaluation\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const hand = sprite\&.getAnimationBoneTransform('hand');
hand\&.rotation += 0\&.2;
sprite\&.setAnimationBoneTransform('hand', hand);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBclearAnimationBoneTransforms()\fP, \fBaddAnimationModifier()\fP 
.RE
.PP

