.SS "\fBSprite\fP setAnimationPhysicsMode (int mode, string bone = \fRundefined\fP, boolean includeDescendants = \fRfalse\fP, number recoveryTime = \fR0\&.5\fP, int direction = \fR\fBrotationDirection_AsSpecified\fP\fP)"

.PP
Select animation control for a physical rig or its bones\&. Kinematic follows the desired animation/IK pose using swept bodies\&. Dynamic releases rig tracking and lets physics determine the pose\&. Driven keeps dynamic bodies and applies bounded tracking forces and torques\&. Mixed is query-only\&. Changing control preserves body, collider and joint identities, mass, velocities and independent scheduled loads\&. Kinematic-to-kinematic joints remain configured but dormant\&. A single selected body can still be restrained by its neighbors\&.

.PP
Selections use the skeleton hierarchy, including skipped bones\&. An included bone may be selected alone; a skipped bone may select included descendants\&. Missing bones or selections with no physical bodies throw\&. The entire selection is validated before any control changes\&. Driven requires configured drive settings on every selected body\&.

.PP
A body has one controller\&. Before rig tracking takes over, release a manual drive with \fBPhysicsBody::clearDrive()\fP, or release a physical \fBPart\fP IK chain with \fBPart::clearIKTarget()\fP\&. To release rig tracking, select Dynamic\&. Raw clearDrive() and manual setDriveTarget() cannot replace rig-owned control\&. Repeated manual setDriveTarget() calls are allowed after release: the last valid call wins\&. Direct mapped-body physics\&.setMode() uses the same coordinator: Dynamic releases rig tracking, Kinematic requests default recovery, and Static throws\&.

.PP
Driven limbs track their desired transform relative to the nearest included physical ancestor\&. Reaction forces and torques act on dynamic parents; free limbs are not independently pinned to world coordinates\&. Bodies without an included ancestor track an animation root target in world coordinates\&. Solver-followed \fBSprite\fP translation does not move that target\&. Rotations use physical body frames, including the reflected reference pose\&. Resolved angular routes persist across ticks; AsSpecified preserves unwrapped turns\&. Physical joint limits remain binding\&.

.PP
Positive recoveryTime blends the requested target from the current physical pose\&. During recovery, the affected bodies remain dynamic and \fBgetAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP reports Driven, including when the destination is Kinematic\&. The requested time is a minimum transition duration: completion waits until position error is within 0\&.1% of segment length (at least 0\&.000001 layer units) and angular error is within 0\&.001 radians\&. Contacts, joint limits or insufficient force may delay completion indefinitely\&. \fBPhysicsBody::getDriveState()\fP reports the target and actual error; normal collision events report contacts\&. There are no recovery-start or blocked events\&. Pausing animation does not pause physical recovery\&.

.PP
Recovery uses bounded integral correction to remove steady gravity/load error, within the same force and torque caps\&. Recovery uses stored drive settings if available\&. For an unconfigured transition to Kinematic only, a temporary 4 Hz, critically damped servo uses force capped at mass * max(segment length, 0\&.001) * (2*pi*4)^2 and torque capped at inertia * (2*pi*4)^2\&. This does not configure the persistent drive-settings record\&. Configure settings explicitly to tune those bounds\&. Zero recoveryTime takes control immediately; Kinematic moves to the requested pose, while Driven starts its bounded drive immediately\&. Dynamic release is always immediate\&.

.PP
Overlapping mode commands cancel the old selection's completion notification; unaffected bodies can finish their existing recovery\&. Any new mode command cancels a pending disable\&. A completed selection emits one Sprite::action_AnimationPhysicsRecoveryComplete event on eventType_SpriteAnimate, with SpriteAnimationPhysicsRecoveryInfo: actingSprite, inLayer, id, bone, wholeRig, includeDescendants, mode, bodyCount and disabled\&. wholeRig means bone is animation_NoBone\&. Immediate takeover completes at the next physics update; disableAnimationPhysics(0) completes synchronously after teardown\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImode\fP animationPhysics_Kinematic, animationPhysics_Dynamic or animationPhysics_Driven\&. 
.br
\fIbone\fP Bone name or current rig bone ID\&. Omit or pass undefined to select the whole rig; explicit null is invalid\&. 
.br
\fIincludeDescendants\fP Include skeletal descendants; default false\&. Whole-rig selection always includes all bodies\&. 
.br
\fIrecoveryTime\fP Finite nonnegative seconds; default 0\&.5\&. 
.br
\fIdirection\fP Rotation route for recovery; default rotationDirection_AsSpecified\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires an active physical rig\&. Call outside pose modifiers and locked solver callbacks\&. Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve active control and recovery state\&. The example assumes a forearm bone\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.setAnimationPhysicsDriveSettings({maxForce: 120, maxTorque: 35}, 'forearm', true);
sprite\&.setAnimationPhysicsMode(pdg\&.animationPhysics_Driven, 'forearm', true);
// Release rig tracking before installing a manual world\-space target\&.
sprite\&.setAnimationPhysicsMode(pdg\&.animationPhysics_Dynamic, 'forearm');
sprite\&.findPart('forearm')\&.physics\&.setDriveTarget(new pdg\&.Point(20, 10), 0, 120, 35);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP, \fBsetAnimationPhysicsDriveSettings()\fP, \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::rotationDirection_AsSpecified\fP\&.
