.SS "\fBSprite\fP setAnimationPhysicsRoot (number bone)"

.PP
Select the bone receiving whole-Sprite impulses and root follow\&. Selection normally prefers the exact name root, otherwise the bone with the most skeletal descendants; ties use the lowest bone ID\&. This call takes precedence\&. Before setup, selecting a zero-length bone gives it the 1 mm fallback on setup\&. For a live generated rig, the bone must have an attached component; disable and select the root before rebuilding if it was previously skipped\&. Live changes preserve component identities and mass\&. Explicitly authored rigs keep the root specified by their definition\&. Invalid selection throws without changing it\&. Root overrides are runtime configuration and are not yet included in snapshots\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbone\fP Bone selector in the current enabled animation rig\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBclearAnimationPhysicsRoot()\fP, \fBgetAnimationPhysicsRoot()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP setAnimationPhysicsRoot (string bone)"

.PP
Select a physical root by its exact bone name\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbone\fP Name in the current enabled animation rig\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
