.SS "setAnimationSource (int source)"

.PP
Select the starting pose for evaluation\&. Clip uses the sampled animation; Reference and Procedural start from the rig reference pose\&. Persistent overrides and modifiers run afterward in every mode\&. Source selection does not create a separate playback clock\&. A change requested inside a callback takes effect after evaluation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIsource\fP \fBpdg\&.animationSource_Clip\fP, \fBpdg\&.animationSource_Reference\fP, or \fBpdg\&.animationSource_Procedural\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAnimationSource()\fP, \fBaddAnimationModifier()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "setDrawHelper (\fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP helper)"

.PP
set a pre-draw helper for custom sprite drawing Sets a helper to do extra drawing stuff for this \fBSprite\fP\&. This helper will be called before the \fBSprite\fP draws normally, and can block normal sprite drawing by returning false from the helper function\&.

.PP
If you want to do overlay effects, use the post-draw helper for that (see \fBsetPostDrawHelper\fP)

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIhelper\fP the pre-draw helper that you want use to add background effects or replace normal rendering of the sprite
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
var myHelper = new pdg\&.ISpriteDrawHelper(function(sprite, port) {
                console\&.log("in my sprite draw helper for " + sprite );
                var r = sprite\&.getLayer()\&.layerToPortRect(sprite\&.getFrameRotatedBounds());
                port\&.fillRect(r, "black");
                port\&.frameRect(r, "white");
                return false;  // don't let sprite draw itself (ignored for post draw)
});
mySprite\&.setDrawHelper(myHelper);
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP 

.PP
\fBsetPostDrawHelper()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP setFrame (int frame)"

.PP
sets the current frame of the sprite to the specified frame number 
.SS "\fBSprite\fP setFrameCollisionMask (\fBImage\fP frameImage, \fBImage\fP maskImage)"

.PP
Assign a mask to frames using an image\&. Retains the mask for every \fBSprite\fP frame using frameImage\&. The alpha frame collider samples it instead of the visible artwork\&. Passing null removes the override\&. A multi-frame mask must contain each referenced frame; a single-frame mask is reused\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIframeImage\fP Artwork image identifying the frames to update\&. 
.br
\fImaskImage\fP Mask image, or null to restore artwork alpha\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP setMouseDetectMode (int collisionType = \fR\fBcollide_BoundingBox\fP\fP)"

.PP
sets the mouse detection mode for this sprite 
.PP
References \fBpdg::collide_BoundingBox\fP\&.
.SS "\fBSprite\fP setOpacity (number opacity)"

.PP
sets the opacity level for this sprite (0\&.0 to 1\&.0) 
.SS "setPostDrawHelper (\fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP helper)"

.PP
sets a helper that draws additional content after the sprite is rendered This function sets a custom drawing helper that will be called after the sprite has been rendered\&. This allows for additional custom drawing operations to be performed on top of the sprite\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIhelper\fP The \fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP object that will handle the post-draw operations
.RE
.PP
The post-draw helper is called after the sprite has been completely rendered, allowing for additional drawing operations such as overlays, effects, or custom graphics to be drawn on top of the sprite\&.

.PP
The helper object must implement the \fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP interface, which provides access to the drawing context and sprite information needed for custom drawing operations\&.

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
The helper will be called every frame while the sprite is visible, so performance should be considered 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The helper has access to the same drawing context as the sprite 

.PP
Setting a new helper will replace any previously set helper
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBISpriteDrawHelper\fP 

.PP
Sprite::setPreDrawHelper() 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupAnimationCollider ()"

.PP
Set up collision geometry that follows active authored animation boxes\&. Reuses or creates \&.collider, preserving its configuration and replacing its geometry source\&. Active boxes follow playback and the final pose\&. Names identify stable shape IDs across disappearance and reappearance\&. Requires an imported animation \fBSprite\fP; unsupported owners/builds throw without changing the association\&. Explicit additions remain active alongside source geometry\&. See \fBcollider_geometry_sources\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The \fBSprite\fP's \fBCollider\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "setupAnimationPhysics (object definition)"

.PP
Create a physical rig for the current pose\&. Validates the definition before creating bodies and joints\&. Creates an ordinary root \fBPhysicsBody\fP if needed, temporarily makes it kinematic, and suspends its collision filter\&. Clip/controller evaluation supplies the desired pose; physical bodies then supply the displayed result\&.

.PP
Each configured bone has a \fBPart\fP named exactly after the bone\&. Obtain it with \fBfindPart()\fP and operate on its \fBPhysicsBody\fP through the read-only \fR\&.\fBphysics\fP\fP property\&. The \fBPart\fP's local transform is the capsule offset from the bone; its world transform follows the solved body\&. Positions and application points use owning-layer coordinates, and velocities use distance units or radians per second\&.

.PP
A pre-existing \fBPart\fP with that name is reused only if it is bound directly to the same bone, has the same capsule offset and unit unreflected scale, has no parent \fBPart\fP, and has neither a \fBPhysicsBody\fP nor a \fBCollider\fP\&. Conflicts reject the configuration without replacing caller-owned Parts\&. While enabled, body mass, inertia, materials, velocities, impulses, forces, torque, damping and drive targets are available through \fR\&.\fBphysics\fP\fP\&. The definition fixes bone bindings and capsule offsets: disable the physical rig before changing those or removing a mapped Part/body\&. Disable keeps the Parts and their names/IDs but returns their \fR\&.\fBphysics\fP\fP properties to NoPhysics\&. Independently retained bodies keep their last state and detach to the basic solver\&.

.PP
Capsules and pivot/rotary-limit joints are shared \fBCollider\fP and \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP components, available through each \fBPart\fP's collider and physics properties\&. The \fBSprite\fP's physics\&.getMass() reports attached component mass; setMass() scales those components proportionally\&. \fBPart\fP mass edits and explicit attach/detach operations update the total without redistributing other masses\&. Whole-Sprite impulses target the selected physical root\&. Contact notifications use the shared \fBColliderContact\fP event; enable them with collider\&.setWantsContactEvents(true)\&. Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve the active rig and its control state\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdefinition\fP Physical rig object described below\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP successfully before using this method\&. The \fBSprite\fP must belong to a physics-enabled \fBSpriteLayer\fP, and \fBsupportsAnimationPhysics()\fP must be true\&. The example assumes a bone named shoulder\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.setupAnimationPhysics({
    bodies: [{ bone: 'shoulder', mass: 1, length: 10, radius: 1 }],
    rootMode: pdg\&.animationRoot_Fixed
});
const shoulder = sprite\&.findPart('shoulder');
const body = shoulder\&.physics;
const state = body\&.getState();
body\&.applyImpulse(new pdg\&.Vector(2, 0), new pdg\&.Point(state\&.x, state\&.y));
body\&.applyTorque(0\&.5, 0\&.25); // torque integrated over a quarter second

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBPhysical animation definition\fP
.RS 4
Top-level field  Default  Meaning  \fRversion\fP  1  Definition format; only integer version 1 is supported\&.  \fRbodies\fP  Required  Nonempty array of body objects (at most 65,536), described below\&. Array indices identify bodies\&.  \fRjoints\fP  []  Array of joint objects (at most 65,536), described below\&.  \fRrootMode\fP  animationRoot_Fixed  Fixed keeps the \fBSprite\fP frame independent; Follow publishes the selected body's translation to the \fBSprite\fP\&. Both support mixed body modes\&.  \fRrootBody\fP  0  Body index used for root follow and release velocity\&.  \fRselfCollisions\fP  false  Whether physical animation bodies may collide with one another\&.  
.RE
.PP
Body field  Default  Meaning  \fRbone\fP  Required  Bone name or ID in the current rig; one body per driven bone\&.  \fRmass\fP, \fRlength\fP, \fRradius\fP  Required  Finite mass > 0, capsule length >= 0, and radius > 0 in rig distance units\&.  \fRmode\fP  animationBody_Dynamic  Dynamic simulation or animationBody_Kinematic following the desired pose\&.  \fRoffsetX\fP, \fRoffsetY\fP, \fRoffsetRotation\fP  0  Bone-local placement; rotation is in radians\&.  \fRfriction\fP  0\&.7  Finite nonnegative contact friction\&.  \fRelasticity\fP  0  Finite bounce coefficient from 0 to 1\&.  \fRcategories\fP, \fRmask\fP  4294967295  Unsigned 32-bit collision category and mask bits\&.  

.PP
Joint field  Default  Meaning  \fRparent\fP, \fRchild\fP  Required  Body indices connected by the joint\&.  \fRparentX\fP, \fRparentY\fP, \fRchildX\fP, \fRchildY\fP  0  Joint anchor positions in the respective body frames\&.  \fRminAngle\fP, \fRmaxAngle\fP  -Math\&.PI, Math\&.PI  Finite relative angular limits in radians\&.  \fRmaxForce\fP  1000000  Finite positive joint force limit\&.  \fRcollide\fP  false  Whether the connected bodies may collide\&.  

.PP
Fixed-root mode keeps the \fBSprite\fP frame authoritative\&. Follow-root mode publishes the selected body's translation while preserving the \fBSprite\fP's rotation and scale\&. The selected body can be Kinematic, Dynamic or Driven\&. \fBSprite\fP movement and rotation edit the animation target frame: controlled root bodies sweep or drive toward it, and dynamic descendants react through their joints\&. Dynamic bodies are not teleported\&. Pose/Part queries between an edit and the next solve do not discard the target, and followed translation does not feed back into a drive target\&. Use scheduled movement/rotation or an animation helper for a continuous path\&.

.PP
The \fBSprite\fP and driven bones require unit effective scale magnitudes; reflection is supported\&. \fR\fBsetFlipX()\fP\fP/\fR\fBsetFlipY()\fP\fP also reflect an active rig about the \fBSprite\fP's local axes through its origin\&. Positions, linear/angular velocities, collider frames, internal anchors, rotary limits and rig recovery state follow the flip\&. Body, collider, shape and constraint identities and mass/inertia are preserved\&. Detached parts remain independent\&. Bone/Part queries, artwork and mounts use the same reflected frames\&. World-space manual drives, IK targets, forces and torques retain their world targets; gravity is unchanged\&.

.PP
External linear joints retain their outside anchors\&. Disconnect external angular joints before flipping; an unsupported boundary joint, a locked solver, or a pose callback rejects the flip without changing it\&. Arbitrary live scaling does not resize physical bodies\&. Create the rig outside callbacks and a locked physics step; existing \fBSprite\fP joints and a second enabled rig are rejected\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP, \fBfindPart()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody::getState()\fP, \fBsupportsAnimationPhysics()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupCollider ()"

.PP
Set up the collision geometry association for this owner\&. An existing collider keeps its geometry and settings; use \&.collider to access it directly\&. A new collider starts enabled with no shapes, no sensor flag and owner-body association\&. Does not create a \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The owned collider\&. Native callers may addRef()/release() to retain it after removal\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupFrameCollider (int mode = \fR\fBframeCollider_AlphaMask\fP\fP, int alphaThreshold = \fR128\fP)"

.PP
Set up collision geometry that follows the current frame\&. Creates the read-only \&.collider association only when absent; otherwise reuses it\&. Preserves enabled/sensor state, filters, material, handlers and body association\&. Every call replaces previous geometry with the selected source and applies the supplied mode and threshold, including their defaults\&. Bounds follow frame dimensions and pivots; alpha mode uses the assigned frame mask or the frame image\&. A \fBSprite\fP without image frames uses its logical bounds\&. Explicit add methods then add persistent geometry; see \fBcollider_geometry_sources\fP\&. Pixel edits to the same image require selecting the source again\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImode\fP frameCollider_AlphaMask (default) or frameCollider_Bounds\&. 
.br
\fIalphaThreshold\fP Integer from 1 through 255, default 128; applies to alpha masks\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The \fBSprite\fP's \fBCollider\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Enable collisions on the owning \fBSpriteLayer\fP for contacts; geometry queries also work without a layer or physics body\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const layer = pdg\&.createSpriteLayer();
layer\&.enableCollisions();
const sprite = layer\&.createSprite();
sprite\&.setSize(24, 40);
const collider = sprite\&.setupFrameCollider(pdg\&.frameCollider_Bounds);
const extra = collider\&.addPolygon([
    new pdg\&.Point(12, \-4), new pdg\&.Point(24, 0), new pdg\&.Point(12, 4)
]);
sprite\&.setSize(30, 40); // The frame shape updates; extra remains\&.
collider\&.removeShape(extra);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::frameCollider_AlphaMask\fP\&.
.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setupPhysicsBody (number mass = \fR1\fP, number momentOfInertia = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Set up the optional physics body with the specified mass and inertia\&. Every call applies both arguments, including their defaults: \fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP sets mass and moment of inertia to 1, and setupPhysicsBody(5) sets mass to 5 and inertia to 1\&. An existing body keeps its identity, transform, velocity, mode, forces, constraints and other settings\&. Read \&.physics to access it without reconfiguration\&. Invalid mass or inertia throws before changing either value\&.

.PP
If absent, creates a dynamic body at the owner's current transform and stops programmed movement/spin\&. Removal detaches retained references; JavaScript keeps them alive automatically\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImass\fP Finite positive mass; default 1\&. 
.br
\fImomentOfInertia\fP Finite positive moment of inertia; default 1\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The owner's \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. The read-only physics property refers to this same object\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Dynamic bodies own movement and rotation\&. Programmed movement/spin requests on their owners throw; immediate setters teleport the body\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const body = sprite\&.setupPhysicsBody(2, 4);
body\&.applyImpulse(new pdg\&.Vector(4, 0));

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremovePhysicsBody()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP setupPhysicsFromAnimationRig (number totalMass, number unitsPerMeter = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Generate a dynamic physical rig from the reference skeleton\&. Creates bone-named Parts with shared PhysicsBodies, capsule Colliders and pivot PhysicsConstraints\&. Bodies start dynamic; the \fBSprite\fP follows the selected root's translation\&. Its coordinating body stays kinematic and does not add simulated mass\&. The initial body pose and velocity come from the current \fBSprite\fP pose/motion\&.

.PP
Geometry uses the pose chosen by \fBenableAnimationPose()\fP\&. A branching bone spans its farthest child connection points; one child gives the span from the bone's own joint to that child\&. A leaf uses the longer axis of its image bounds' union in bone-local coordinates, including reference transforms and pivots\&. Bounds use authored SCML image dimensions\&. Missing artwork is diagnosed and skipped\&. Other zero-length segments are skipped, except the selected root: it receives a 1 mm physical segment converted with unitsPerMeter\&. The authored skeleton is unchanged\&. Lengths are measured after reference bone scaling\&. Capsule radius is 10% of that physical length\&. Generated Parts expose a rigid body frame in layer distance units, so nonuniform bone display scales do not deform the capsules\&. Local/Sprite transform queries convert that same rigid frame into the requested space\&. Included segment lengths determine mass fractions; the coordinating body and unrelated Parts are excluded\&.

.PP
Each included child connects to its nearest included ancestor at the child's current joint location\&. Distinct skeletal trees remain separate components\&. Pivots have unlimited strength, no break threshold and free rotation\&. Components share a nonzero collision group to suppress internal contacts; callers can edit their filters\&. There are no automatically inferred angular limits or drives\&.

.PP
Repeated setup requires the original membership (all generated Parts, no added accessories); edited membership must first be restored\&. It reapplies the original mass fractions, scaling inertia proportionally while keeping bodies, colliders, joints, edited geometry, velocity and independent loads\&. Changing unitsPerMeter or switching from an explicit definition requires \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP first\&. Ordinary physics\&.setMass() preserves the current, possibly tuned, mass fractions instead\&. An existing bone-named \fBPart\fP must have the same binding/offset, no parent, unit unreflected local scale, and no body or collider\&. Conflicts throw before replacing caller-owned associations\&. Mapped offsets/bindings and \fBPart\fP removal remain fixed until disabled\&. Change body control with \fBsetAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP\&. Edit physical properties and geometry through the \fBPart\fP's physics/collider objects; changing geometry does not recalculate inertia\&.

.PP
The \fBSprite\fP's physics\&.getMass() reports component mass; physics\&.setMass() scales all component masses and inertia atomically\&. Individual mass edits change the total without redistributing\&. Whole-Sprite linear/angular impulses target the selected root, including the world-point lever arm\&. Velocities, continuous forces/torques and manual drives should be applied to the component bodies\&. Single-body setupPhysicsBody(mass, inertia) and aggregate setMomentOfInertia() reject while this rig is active\&. Inertia/angular-momentum queries on the \fBSprite\fP still describe its coordinating body, not a pose-dependent assembly sum\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItotalMass\fP Finite positive mass in application mass units\&. 
.br
\fIunitsPerMeter\fP Finite positive number of layer distance units per meter; default 1 means meter coordinates for the fallback conversion\&. For example, 1000 makes the 1 mm fallback one layer unit\&. Other authored dimensions are already in layer/rig units and are not converted by this argument\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBSprite\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires an enabled animation pose, Chipmunk support and a physics-enabled \fBSpriteLayer\fP\&. Configure the layer before adding Sprites\&. Bone scales must be nonsingular; nonuniform authored bone scales and reflected initial poses are supported\&. The \fBSprite\fP root needs uniform scale\&. Set \fBSprite\fP scale/flip before setup: dynamic physical bones keep their initial effective scales while enabled\&. Call outside pose modifiers and locked solver callbacks\&. Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve active rigs, edited components, membership and control/recovery state\&. The example assumes a bone named forearm and successful pose setup\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.setupPhysicsFromAnimationRig(70);
sprite\&.findPart('forearm')\&.physics\&.setMass(3); // changes the total
sprite\&.physics\&.setMass(80); // scales the current distribution
sprite\&.physics\&.applyImpulse(new pdg\&.Vector(20, 0));

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindPart()\fP, \fBsetAnimationPhysicsRoot()\fP, \fBgetAnimationPhysicsSetupWarnings()\fP, \fBdisableAnimationPhysics()\fP 
.RE
.PP

