enables or disables offscreen event generation for this sprite 
.SS "startAnimation (int animationId)"

.PP
Start playing an animation by its ID\&. Selects the clip and resumes playback at its retained clip time\&. This is not a seek to zero\&. Cancels any unfinished blend and clears paused state\&. Invalid names/IDs leave playback unchanged\&. 
.SS "startAnimation (string animationName)"

.PP
Start playing an animation by its name\&. Selects the clip and resumes playback at its retained clip time\&. This is not a seek to zero\&. Cancels any unfinished blend and clears paused state\&. Invalid names/IDs leave playback unchanged\&. 
.SS "startFrameAnimation (number fps, int startingFrame = \fR\fBstart_FromFirstFrame\fP\fP, int numFrames = \fR\fBall_Frames\fP\fP, int animateFlags = \fR\fBanimate_Looping\fP\fP)"

.PP
starts frame animation with specified fps, starting frame, number of frames, and animation flags 
.PP
References \fBpdg::all_Frames\fP, \fBpdg::animate_Looping\fP, and \fBpdg::start_FromFirstFrame\fP\&.
.SS "stopAnimation ()"

.PP
stops the current animation and pauses playback For compatibility, stopAnimation pauses at the current pose\&. It does not reset time or cancel an active blend; resumeAnimation continues playback\&. 
.SS "stopFrameAnimation ()"

.PP
stops all frame animation, keeping the current frame as the sprite's image 
.SS "boolean supportsAnimationPhysics ()"

.PP
Test this build's physical-animation support\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Animation physics requires Chipmunk\&. The Basic solver supports simple shared-body physics but is intentionally not a backend for animation rigs; expanding it to complex animation physics is not planned\&. Enable Chipmunk on the \fBSpriteLayer\fP before rig setup\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True when built with Chipmunk physics support\&. This does not test the \fBSprite\fP's current layer, rig, or scale\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetupAnimationPhysics()\fP, \fBisAnimationPhysicsEnabled()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP transferPart (\fBPart\fP part, boolean includeDescendants = \fRtrue\fP)"

.PP
Transfer an existing \fBPart\fP and optional subtree into this \fBSprite\fP\&. Moves the same \fBPart\fP objects; retained \fBPart\fP, \fBPhysicsBody\fP, \fBCollider\fP and internal \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handles remain valid\&. Names and Part-owned Image/Drawing content are retained\&. The destination assigns fresh per-Sprite IDs and appends the moved Parts in their source order\&. Read getId() again after transfer\&. Transferring a \fBPart\fP already owned by this \fBSprite\fP is a no-op\&.

.PP
World transforms, body mass/inertia, velocities, loads, manual world-space drives and collision settings are preserved\&. The moved root loses its old \fBPart\fP parent; parents inside the transferred set are retained\&. With includeDescendants false, children left behind keep their world placement and nearest remaining \fBPart\fP ancestor\&. Movement, rotation and scale programming is canceled on Parts whose parent frame changes\&. Logical size animation and other local state remain\&.

.PP
Descendants include ordinary \fBPart\fP children, physical-rig bone descendants and registered assembly children\&. Joints within the selected set survive\&. Joints to any body outside it disconnect; retained handles report inactive\&. Source assembly mass decreases by the transferred member masses without redistributing the others\&. The destination does not automatically register the transferred bodies in its rig: use \fBattachAnimationPhysicsPart()\fP and create any new joints explicitly\&.

.PP
Mapped rig bodies are released from the source controller and become ordinary Dynamic \fBPart\fP bodies\&. At least one attached skeletal body must remain in the source rig; transferring its selected root chooses a remaining root using the usual rule\&. Source bone/artwork/socket bindings are cleared rather than rebound by name\&. The source skeleton, animation clips, imported artwork and animation-drawing registrations remain source-owned; use \fBPart\&.setDrawing()\fP/setImage() for artwork that moves with the \fBPart\fP\&. The source rig can subsequently be disabled or destroyed without removing the transferred bodies\&. Layer snapshots preserve the resulting ownership and joints\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpart\fP \fBPart\fP currently owned by a \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.br
\fIincludeDescendants\fP Transfer descendants too; optional, default true\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The same \fBPart\fP, now owned by this \fBSprite\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Both Sprites must share a layer, or both be off-layer\&. Names must be unique in the destination\&. Singular/sheared placements that cannot be represented by \fBPart\fP transforms and Sprite-mount cycles reject before transfer\&. Call outside animation modifiers, drawing callbacks and locked physics callbacks\&. Finish or cancel source rig recovery first\&. Clear any \fBPart\fP IK target involving a selected \fBPart\fP; re-establish it after transfer\&. Release manual drives before detaching attached skeletal bodies, following the existing explicit drive-handoff contract\&. Independent or already detached bodies retain their manual drives\&. Parent-relative IK limits are cleared when their frame changes\&. The example assumes a physical weight \fBPart\fP and a hand in the receiving \fBSprite\fP's active rig\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
